# jaws_le 1.02 - drafted by port_tool.py from godzilla_pro-1.15.port, finished by hand (item 136).
# The first port for a title with its own rules code. What was placed by hand, what the
# emulator proved, and what is still copied is written beside each entry.
# Proven in the emulator (PAD_CARD jaws_le-1_02_0, muted): all 24 functions match; the
# shot dispatch, tick and ball end hooks fire (one thread); template_mode.c runs unchanged.
# Emulator-proven 2026-09-24 by a full build check (modes/gamecheck.sh play full, item 162): the
# runtime hooked the game, 26 of its 27 shots came from their switches, a drain ended each ball, and
# the 7 events below fired where their names say (a tilted ball, three balls to the game's end).
# Shots no press made (their switch is left out of the check, or needs two): Mid flipper lane.
# Callouts heard in the emulator 2026-09-24 (item 163): countdown, ten_seconds, time_up.

game           jaws_le
version        1.02

# ---- functions: site <name> <address> <first two instruction words> --------------------
# hooked by the runtime
#   tick: located (strict)
site tick             0x002b7298 0xe92d4038 0xe3a00037
#   shot_dispatch: by hand (item 136) - cmode_manager virtual 11, called once from the shot handler with the mask in r2:r3
site shot_dispatch    0x0014f938 0xe92d4ff0 0xe3045b18
#   ball_end: 0x1521e8, which the handler of hook 0x34 calls (item 138). Item 136's loose match, 0x1524cc,
#   was a sibling loop over the same modes calling another virtual: it ran once at game start
site ball_end         0x001521e8 0xe92d40f8 0xe30e6c04
#   sound_lookup: located (strict)
site sound_lookup     0x0055bab8 0xe92d4038 0xe1a05000
# called
#   score_add: located (strict)
site score_add        0x003d3260 0xe3041d0e 0xe3401087
#   callout: by hand (item 136) - the framework request Godzilla's wrapper ends in; Jaws calls it directly 366 times
site callout          0x004c2fe0 0xe92d4010 0xe30ceda8
#   callout_nth: by hand (item 136) - the framework numbered request; cmode_timed's countdown tail-calls it
site callout_nth      0x004c3194 0xe92d4010 0xe30ceda8
#   light_run: located (strict)
site light_run        0x0028f67c 0xeafffd83 0xe92d40f0
